		<h1>Software Acceleration Team of KSU</h1>
		<h2>Introduction</h2>
		<p>
			SwAT exists to accelerate the education of computing students at Kennesaw
			State University. We do this in three ways:
			<ul>
				<li>
					Workshops and knowledge sessions on the skills and tools most CS and
					software engineering programs skip (or leave until much later), in the
					spirit of MIT’s Missing Semester.
				</li>
				<li>
					Team projects on non-trivial software that students must fully
					understand, then present and defend in review sessions. This gives
					students practical work experience: they will use proper version
					control practices, create and run CI/CD pipelines, and code
					collaboratively with teammates.
				</li>
				<li>Early connections between students and industry professionals.</li>
			</ul>
			Along the way, students gain more than technical skill: they learn to work in
			teams, lead, and present their work. We reward students with a bias for action
			by letting them run the projects and sessions they care about, so they graduate
			as capable engineers, ready to confidently work and lead in the field.
		</p>
