		<h3>Recent Projects</h3>
		<p>
			WASM Primes Students/contributors explore rendering prime number spirals
			in the browser starting with a simple TypeScript and HTML Canvas
			implementation and building up towards higher-performance technologies.
			The proect will cover generating prime numbers, mapping them onto a
			spiral, and drawing the result with the Canvas API. From there, it will
			evolve through progressively more advanced implementations, including
			WebAssumbly and WebGL. The goal is to use the same problem to learn and
			compare different approaches to computation and rendering on the wen,
			through an interactive medium.
			<br /><br />
			The planned progression includes:
			<ul>
				<li>1. TypeScript + HTML Canvas</li>
				<li>2. Interactive Visualization</li>
				<li>3. Performance Improvements</li>
				<li>4. WebGL</li>
				<li>5. WebAssembly + Rust</li>
			</ul>
			The end result will be an interactive prime spiral visualization, but the primary
			purpose of the project is to explore how the same porblem can be approached
			at progressively different levels of the web stack.
			<br /><br />
			Starting with simple TypeScript and Canvas code and eventuallly reaching Rust,
			WebAssembly, and WebGL will provide a practical way to learn about language
			boundaries, compilation, bundling, browser performance, GPU rendering, and the
			architecture of modern web applications.
		</p>
